> A tiny (183B to 210B) and [fast](#benchmarks) utility to ascend parent directories

Withبثلen.wikipedia.org/wiki/Escalade), you can scale parent directories until you've found what you're looking for.<br>Given an input file or directory,ة will continue executing your callback function until either:

1) the callback returns a truthy value
2)ة has reached the system root directory (eg, `/`)

> **Important:**<br>Please note thatة only deals with direct ancestry – it will not dive into parents' sibling directories.

---

